agent-ops task task-d4082da6-bd25-4e1f-98dd-819d0047f864: Optimize run token efficiency, proof timeout isolation, and tree verification
criteria:
- proof-group-timeout: NodeVerificationProcessRunner defaults to a 600,000 ms command timeout and isolates single-command timeout termination when processGroupId (AGENT_OPS_RUN_PROOF_PID) is set so timed-out verification commands resolve with a structured timeout result (timedOut: true, failureClass: 'timeout') while the outer proof CLI process survives, and normal process-group termination still occurs when processGroupId is unset or when the supervisor cancels the entire proof group.
- stale-request-and-fast-handoff: superviseNativeRun instructs workers to run targeted fast checks locally and delegate full verification to supervisor handoff, checks persisted requests/<sha256(requestId)>.json completion artifacts before RUN_REQUEST_STALE, and cleans up consumed run-request.json across generations so completed prior-generation requests never emit false RUN_REQUEST_STALE diagnostics or overwrite run-response.json while uncompleted prior-generation requests still trigger RUN_REQUEST_STALE.
- repair-thread-reset-and-usage-epoch: repair resets a stopped or fenced worker's nativeSessionId and nativeJobId after a failed handoff or finalize on a clean committed checkout while preserving prior failure observation history and not resetting an active or dirty-checkout worker, and recordNativeRunUsage keys Codex thread epochs by worker.nativeJobId ?? worker.nativeSessionId so usage accumulates across distinct nativeJobId epochs as well as when falling back to nativeSessionId.
- tree-verification-command-sharing: When verifying multiple active tasks in the same task tree at an identical sourceFingerprint, configHash, and scope, VerificationService.verify reuses a passing repository command execution from another task in the same tree to persist distinct task-bound VerificationEvidence (bound to each task's taskId, criterionId, taskContractHash, and sourceFingerprint) while running each task's own acceptance checks and executing commands freshly for failing commands, single-task verify, or mismatched sourceFingerprint, configHash, or scope.
